WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.652
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level C one.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:09.408
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:17.736
Unit twenty-seven: Passive Gerunds and Infinitives. Today you will use passive forms after verbs of feeling and necessity.

4
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:20.595
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:24.627
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:26.438
Being done.

7
00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.519
Being done means a passive gerund.

8
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:31.896
I hate being told what to do.

9
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:35.205
Your turn. Say: Being done.

10
00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:39.671
Being done.

11
00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:41.418
To be done.

12
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:44.765
To be done means a passive infinitive.

13
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:46.908
The work needs to be done.

14
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:50.471
Your turn. Say: To be done.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.323
To be done.

16
00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:56.282
Having been done.

17
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.910
Having been done means a perfect passive gerund.

18
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.180
He denied having been warned.

19
00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:06.028
Your turn. Say: Having been done.

20
00:01:08.867 --> 00:01:10.204
Having been done.

21
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:12.276
To have been done.

22
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:16.757
To have been done means a perfect passive infinitive.

23
00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:18.920
It seems to have been forgotten.

24
00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:22.332
Your turn. Say: To have been done.

25
00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:26.295
To have been done.

26
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.318
Passive gerund.

27
00:01:29.317 --> 00:01:32.384
Passive gerund means being + past participle.

28
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:34.402
A passive gerund.

29
00:01:35.017 --> 00:01:37.971
Your turn. Say: Passive gerund.

30
00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.148
Passive gerund.

31
00:01:42.883 --> 00:01:44.256
Passive infinitive.

32
00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.585
Passive infinitive means to be + past participle.

33
00:01:49.183 --> 00:01:50.916
A passive infinitive.

34
00:01:51.517 --> 00:01:55.109
Your turn. Say: Passive infinitive.

35
00:01:57.967 --> 00:01:59.746
Passive infinitive.

36
00:02:00.483 --> 00:02:01.891
Perfect passive.

37
00:02:02.883 --> 00:02:06.241
Perfect passive means having been / to have been + participle.

38
00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.374
A perfect passive.

39
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:11.729
Your turn. Say: Perfect passive.

40
00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.812
Perfect passive.

41
00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:17.330
Agent.

42
00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:20.746
Agent means the person who does the action.

43
00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.013
The agent is not mentioned.

44
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:25.839
Your turn. Say: Agent.

45
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.504
Agent.

46
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.241
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:40.879
Visal, which sounds better: I hate people telling me what to do, or I hate being told what to do?

48
00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:55.131
The second is more natural when we focus on the receiver. Being told is a passive gerund, formed by being + past participle after verbs like hate, enjoy, avoid and deny.

49
00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:57.647
And with infinitives?

50
00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:11.587
To be + participle follows verbs of need and expectation: The report needs to be finished. She expects to be promoted. The agent is often unknown or unimportant.

51
00:03:12.683 --> 00:03:14.393
What about an earlier action?

52
00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:26.765
Use having been or to have been: He denied having been warned. The vase seems to have been broken. These perfect passives refer to a time before the main verb.

53
00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.203
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:36.844
Grammar focus: Passive forms: being and having been plus participle; to be and to have been plus participle.

55
00:03:37.144 --> 00:03:38.285
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:38.983 --> 00:03:40.739
I hate being told what to do.

57
00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.684
The work needs to be finished today.

58
00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:46.223
He denied having been warned.

59
00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:55.789
After verbs of feeling use being + participle. After need or expect use to be + participle. Use having been / to have been for earlier actions.

60
00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.387
Be careful! Don't say: I hate to be told what to do.

61
00:04:02.333 --> 00:04:04.612
Say: I hate being told what to do.

62
00:04:04.912 --> 00:04:06.435
Use a passive gerund.

63
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:09.758
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:11.951
Receiving the Action.

65
00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:14.866
I dislike being interrupted when I am speaking.

66
00:04:15.867 --> 00:04:18.319
The new rules need to be explained clearly.

67
00:04:19.333 --> 00:04:22.088
She was delighted at having been chosen for the team.

68
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.657
The vase seems to have been broken during the move.

69
00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:29.688
The passive focuses on what happens to the receiver.

70
00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:34.825
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:35.683 --> 00:04:37.346
I hate blank what to do.

72
00:04:37.646 --> 00:04:41.416
A, being told. B, telling. C, to tell.

73
00:04:44.967 --> 00:04:47.268
The answer is A: being told.

74
00:04:48.417 --> 00:04:50.219
The work needs blank today.

75
00:04:50.519 --> 00:04:54.288
A, to be finished. B, finishing. C, to finish.

76
00:04:57.833 --> 00:04:59.775
The answer is A: to be finished.

77
00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:02.591
He denied blank warned.

78
00:05:02.891 --> 00:05:05.964
A, being. B, having been. C, to be.

79
00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.546
The answer is B: having been.

80
00:05:12.683 --> 00:05:14.834
To have been broken refers to blank.

81
00:05:15.134 --> 00:05:19.217
A, an earlier time. B, the future. C, a habit.

82
00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:25.231
The answer is A: an earlier time.

83
00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:29.138
According to the reading, what happened to the vase?

84
00:05:29.438 --> 00:05:33.439
A, it was broken. B, it was sold. C, it was cleaned.

85
00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.290
The answer is A: it was broken.

86
00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.675
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:44.517 --> 00:05:48.513
Write a sentence using 'being' + past participle after a verb of feeling.

88
00:05:57.317 --> 00:05:58.666
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:58.966 --> 00:06:10.514
I really enjoy being praised when I work hard. I dislike being ignored in a group. The passive gerund focuses on what happens to me and not on who does it.

90
00:06:10.814 --> 00:06:12.489
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:13.383 --> 00:06:22.143
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive forms: being and having been plus participle; to be and to have been plus participle.

92
00:06:22.443 --> 00:06:28.276
Today's value is reflective awareness. Notice your own experience with care and honesty.

93
00:06:28.576 --> 00:06:31.286
See you in Unit twenty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:06:31.586 --> 00:06:34.622
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

